markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Classroom Context

#### This is the second unit of the course, building off the content from unit one. The course was designed to teach in order.

#### Teachers serve as guides supporting **design thinking, encouraging responsible AI use, and helping students interpret and improve AI-generated work**.


## Unit Length and Format

#### **Total Duration:** Approximately 3 weeks
#### **Structure:** Eleven 45-minute lessons and one 3-day culminating project

<img src="https://images.code.org/90238cb17488ca22b7bcaa13be5ebf64-image-1767899047978.png" alt="lesson calandar for unit 2" width="650px" style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;border-radius:10px; ">

## **Lesson Flow:**


<!-- Simplified Lesson Flow Table (All text 14pt) -->
<table style="width:100%; max-width:800px; border-collapse:collapse; font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:14pt; line-height:1.4;">

  <tr>
    <th style="border:2px solid #000; padding:10px; text-align:left; width:30%;font-size:14pt;">Phase</th>
    <th style="border:2px solid #000; padding:10px; text-align:left;font-size:14pt;">Summary</th>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="border:2px solid #000; padding:10px; font-weight:bold;font-size:14pt;">Early Lessons</td>
    <td style="border:2px solid #000; padding:10px;font-size:14pt;">
      Students learn interactivity and event-driven programming by exploring how user actions control app behavior and practicing debugging with AI support.
    </td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="border:2px solid #000; padding:10px; font-weight:bold;font-size:14pt;">Mid-Unit Lessons</td>
    <td style="border:2px solid #000; padding:10px;font-size:14pt;">
      Students use variables, functions, and conditional logic to plan and build dynamic interactions using flowcharts and reusable code.
    </td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="border:2px solid #000; padding:10px; font-weight:bold;font-size:14pt;">Final Project</td>
    <td style="border:2px solid #000; padding:10px;font-size:14pt;">
      Students design, build, and refine a fully interactive web app that responds to users in real time, using AI-assisted debugging.
    </td>
  </tr>

</table>



## Next up

#### Let's dive into the instructional commitments for this course. 



